 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Make a warm welcome with a card before they arrive. Which rooms they' be in, and how many people there will be. A little of both is nice. A plate with biscuits, a water glass, and a few glasses for drinks gives the idea of being lived in. A short note is fine. A card is easier to find reason back for later if you use it as a crime scene. A small bouquet of fresh ones says you lived here without feeling like guest. And roses look grand but they' expensive.",
